/*!
\page page_stemccollection StEmcCollection — EMC Collection Documentation

\section emc_overview Overview

The STAR Electromagnetic Calorimeter (EMC) detects photons, electrons, and positrons by
measuring electromagnetic shower energy in lead-scintillator sampling calorimeters.
It is divided into two physical systems:

- <b>Barrel EMC (BEMC)</b> — covers |η| < 1, full azimuth.  Four sub-detectors:
  towers (energy), preshower (BPRS), and two Shower Maximum Detector (SMD) planes segmented
  in η (BSMDE) and φ (BSMDP).
- <b>Endcap EMC (EEMC)</b> — covers 1 < η < 2.  Analogous structure: towers, preshower
  (EPRS), and SMD planes (ESMDU, ESMDV).

\ref StEmcCollection is the single top-level object saved in \c StEvent for all EMC data.
It aggregates per-sub-detector \ref StEmcDetector objects, global reconstructed points, and
raw DAQ data banks.  Cluster data live one level deeper inside each \ref StEmcDetector via
an owned \ref StEmcClusterCollection.

\section emc_classes Classes in this group

| Class | Role |
|-------|------|
| \ref StEmcCollection | Top-level event container for all EMC sub-detectors, points, and raw data |
| \ref StEmcClusterCollection | Per-sub-detector container for reconstructed EMC clusters |

Related classes (not documented here):

| Class | Role |
|-------|------|
| \ref StEmcDetector | One EMC sub-detector; holds modules, raw hits, and a cluster collection |
| \ref StEmcModule | One readout module within a sub-detector; holds raw hits |
| \ref StEmcCluster | A reconstructed cluster of adjacent hits |
| \ref StEmcPoint | Higher-level object combining clusters from multiple sub-detectors |
| \c StEmcRawData | Raw DAQ data banks for BEMC or EEMC |

\section emc_indexing Sub-detector array indexing

\ref StEmcCollection stores sub-detector objects in \c mDetector[8], a fixed-size array of
raw pointers.  The array index is computed as \c (StDetectorId - kBarrelEmcTowerId).
Identifier integer values are defined in \c StDetectorDefinitions.h.

| Array index | \c StDetectorId | Integer | Physical sub-detector |
|-------------|-----------------|---------|----------------------|
| 0 | \c kBarrelEmcTowerId | 9 | BEMC towers (energy measurement) |
| 1 | \c kBarrelEmcPreShowerId | 10 | BEMC preshower (BPRS) |
| 2 | \c kBarrelSmdEtaStripId | 11 | BEMC SMD η strips (BSMDE) |
| 3 | \c kBarrelSmdPhiStripId | 12 | BEMC SMD φ strips (BSMDP) |
| 4 | \c kEndcapEmcTowerId | 13 | EEMC towers (energy measurement) |
| 5 | \c kEndcapEmcPreShowerId | 14 | EEMC preshower (EPRS) |
| 6 | \c kEndcapSmdUStripId | 15 | EEMC SMD U strips (ESMDU) |
| 7 | \c kEndcapSmdVStripId | 16 | EEMC SMD V strips (ESMDV) |

\ref StEmcCollection::detector returns \c nullptr for any ID outside the range
[\c kBarrelEmcTowerId, \c kEndcapSmdVStripId].

\section emc_hierarchy Containment hierarchy

\code{.unparsed}
StEmcCollection                                       (1 per event, in StEvent)
├── mDetector[8]  (StEmcDetector*, heap-allocated, indexed by StDetectorId offset)
│   ├── mModules[120] (StEmcModule*, 1-based, heap-allocated by StEmcDetector)
│   │   └── mHits     (StSPtrVecEmcRawHit — owns StEmcRawHit objects)
│   └── mClusters     (StEmcClusterCollection*, heap-allocated, owned by StEmcDetector)
│       └── mClusters (StSPtrVecEmcCluster — owns StEmcCluster objects)
├── mBarrel        (StSPtrVecEmcPoint — owns barrel StEmcPoint objects)
├── mEndcap        (StSPtrVecEmcPoint — owns endcap StEmcPoint objects)
├── mBemcRawData   (StEmcRawData*, heap-allocated, owned by StEmcCollection)
└── mEemcRawData   (StEmcRawData*, heap-allocated, owned by StEmcCollection)
\endcode

\section emc_ownership Object Ownership

\subsection emc_own_coll StEmcCollection
\c mDetector[8] holds raw pointers to heap-allocated \ref StEmcDetector objects.  The
destructor deletes every non-null element.  \c mBemcRawData and \c mEemcRawData are
deleted by the destructor as well.  \c mBarrel and \c mEndcap are \c StSPtrVecEmcPoint
owning vectors; their elements are automatically deleted via \c StStrArray on destruction.

The copy constructor and assignment operator are \b private — \ref StEmcCollection is
non-copyable.

\warning Do not delete \ref StEmcDetector, \ref StEmcPoint, or \c StEmcRawData objects
obtained from this collection.

\subsection emc_own_cluster StEmcClusterCollection
\c mClusters is a \c StSPtrVecEmcCluster owning vector.  \c StStrArray automatically
deletes the \ref StEmcCluster objects when the vector is destroyed.  The
\ref StEmcClusterCollection destructor is an explicit no-op.

\warning Do not delete \ref StEmcCluster objects obtained from
\ref StEmcClusterCollection::clusters.

\section emc_members Data Members

\subsection emc_mem_coll StEmcCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StEmcDetector*[8] | \c mDetector | Per-sub-detector objects, indexed by \c (StDetectorId - kBarrelEmcTowerId) |
| \c StSPtrVecEmcPoint | \c mBarrel | Reconstructed points in the Barrel EMC (BEMC) |
| \c StSPtrVecEmcPoint | \c mEndcap | Reconstructed points in the Endcap EMC (EEMC) |
| \c StEmcRawData* | \c mBemcRawData | Raw DAQ data banks for the BEMC |
| \c StEmcRawData* | \c mEemcRawData | Raw DAQ data banks for the EEMC |

\subsection emc_mem_cluster StEmcClusterCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StDetectorId | \c mDetector | Identifier of the sub-detector owning these clusters |
| \c StSPtrVecEmcCluster | \c mClusters | Owned vector of reconstructed \ref StEmcCluster objects |
| \c Int_t | \c mClusterFinderId | Cluster-finder algorithm identifier |
| \c Int_t | \c mClusterFinderParamVersion | Cluster-finder parameter version |

\section emc_methods Key Methods

\subsection emc_meth_coll StEmcCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c StEmcDetector* \c detector(StDetectorId) | Sub-detector for the given ID; \c nullptr if out of range |
| \c StSPtrVecEmcPoint& \c barrelPoints() | Mutable reference to the barrel point list |
| \c StSPtrVecEmcPoint& \c endcapPoints() | Mutable reference to the endcap point list |
| \c StEmcRawData* \c bemcRawData() | Raw DAQ data for the BEMC |
| \c StEmcRawData* \c eemcRawData() | Raw DAQ data for the EEMC |
| \c void \c setDetector(StEmcDetector*) | Register a sub-detector (takes ownership; replaces the existing slot if non-null) |
| \c void \c addBarrelPoint(const \c StEmcPoint*) | Append a point to the barrel list |
| \c void \c addEndcapPoint(const \c StEmcPoint*) | Append a point to the endcap list |
| \c void \c setBemcRawData(StEmcRawData*) | Set BEMC raw data pointer (takes ownership) |
| \c void \c setEemcRawData(StEmcRawData*) | Set EEMC raw data pointer (takes ownership) |

\subsection emc_meth_cluster StEmcClusterCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c StDetectorId \c detector() \c const | Sub-detector identifier |
| \c void \c setDetector(StDetectorId) | Set sub-detector identifier |
| \c int \c numberOfClusters() \c const | Number of clusters in the collection |
| \c StSPtrVecEmcCluster& \c clusters() | Mutable reference to the cluster vector |
| \c const \c StSPtrVecEmcCluster& \c clusters() \c const | Read-only reference |
| \c void \c addCluster(StEmcCluster*) | Append a cluster (takes ownership) |
| \c int \c clusterFinderId() \c const | Cluster-finder algorithm identifier |
| \c int \c clusterFinderParamVersion() \c const | Cluster-finder parameter version |
| \c void \c setClusterFinderId(int) | Set cluster-finder algorithm identifier |
| \c void \c setClusterFinderParamVersion(int) | Set cluster-finder parameter version |

\section emc_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
// Access BEMC tower clusters
const StEmcCollection* emcColl = event->emcCollection();
if (!emcColl) return;

const StEmcDetector* bemcTowers = emcColl->detector(kBarrelEmcTowerId);
if (bemcTowers) {
    const StEmcClusterCollection* clColl = bemcTowers->cluster();
    if (clColl) {
        const StSPtrVecEmcCluster& clusters = clColl->clusters();
        for (const StEmcCluster* cl : clusters) {
            // cl->energy(), cl->eta(), cl->phi(), etc.
        }
    }
}

// Access all BEMC tower raw hits (module loop, 1-based)
if (bemcTowers) {
    for (unsigned int iMod = 1; iMod <= bemcTowers->numberOfModules(); ++iMod) {
        const StEmcModule* mod = bemcTowers->module(iMod);
        if (!mod) continue;
        for (const StEmcRawHit* rh : mod->hits()) {
            // rh->energy(), rh->adc(), etc.
        }
    }
}

// Iterate over barrel reconstructed points
for (const StEmcPoint* pt : emcColl->barrelPoints()) {
    // pt->energy(), pt->position(), etc.
}
\endcode

*/
